## 2. msg.data and Calldata

### calldata vs memory

```solidity
// calldata - read-only, cheaper for external functions
function process(bytes calldata data) external {
    // data is read-only, cannot modify
    // Cheaper gas for large inputs
}

// memory - mutable, required for internal manipulation
function process(bytes memory data) external {
    data[0] = 0x00;  // Can modify
    // More expensive for large inputs
}
```

### msg.data Length Checks

```solidity
// VULNERABLE - doesn't validate full calldata
function processCalldata() external {
    // Attacker can append extra data
    // Some protocols use extra data for bypass
}

// SECURE - validate expected length
function processCalldata() external {
    require(msg.data.length == 4 + 32, "Invalid calldata");
    // Or use:
    require(msg.data.length == 4 + abi.decode.length);
}
```

