## 7. Contract Creation

### Create vs Create2

```solidity
// CREATE - address depends on deployer nonce
address newContract = address(new MyContract());
// address = keccak256(rlp([sender, nonce]))[12:]

// CREATE2 - deterministic address
bytes32 salt = keccak256("salt");
address newContract = address(new MyContract{salt: salt}());
// address = keccak256(0xff ++ sender ++ salt ++ keccak256(bytecode))[12:]

// SECURITY: With CREATE2, same bytecode + salt = same address
// Even if contract is destroyed, can redeploy same address!
```

### Metamorphic Contracts

```solidity
// VULNERABLE - trusting CREATE2 addresses
// Attacker can:
// 1. Deploy contract A at address X
// 2. Contract A selfdestructs
// 3. Deploy different contract B at same address X
// 4. Users think they're interacting with A, but it's B!

// SECURE - check code hash, not just address
bytes32 expectedHash = keccak256(type(ExpectedContract).runtimeCode);
require(keccak256(target.code) == expectedHash, "Wrong code");
```

